; C7  Winning 42 pp. 45-46 (W42-p045-e, W42-p046-a); played in Hand 32,
; p. 109 (W42-p109-b)
; Rule, in our words: a setter who plays right after the bidder, cannot follow
; the bidder's lead, and holds count, plays the count at once, before knowing
; whether the partner can take the trick.
; Python gate (pour_setter gate_c7): seat left of the bidder, the bidder led,
; mover cannot follow, holds a non-trump count tile; every such tile is the
; book's.
; How this encoding differs: none from the gate. The gate (and this file) also
; fires on a trump lead; the book speaks of the bidder's off. The book's wider
; companion rule (pp. 43-44, W42-p043-i: with no double, play count even when
; you can follow) is played in Hand 28 (p. 98) and is not in the gate.
; GAP declarer: the bidder is written in as S0, the left seat as S1.
(policy c07-pounce
  (initial play)
  (fallback lowest-legal)
  (rule play-count-now (in play) (next play) (select answer)
    (guard
      (query
        (roles (domino give) (context led))
        (out give)
        (pattern
          (viewer S1)
          (leader S0)
          (led-context led)
          (own-legal give)
          (not (in give led))
          (not (in give q*))
          (count give 10))
        (pattern
          (viewer S1)
          (leader S0)
          (led-context led)
          (own-legal give)
          (not (in give led))
          (not (in give q*))
          (count give 5))))))
